# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# ./bindings is GENERATED (cargo test --features ts) but deliberately COMMITTED, not ignored.
# It is the published surface of this package (package.json "files") and the frontend resolves
# @chordia/contracts straight to ./index.ts, which re-exports every file in there. Ignoring it broke
# three things at once, silently: frontend CI could not typecheck (TS2307 on all 193 re-exports),
# this repo's own check-bindings step crashed with ENOENT, and the "did you forget to regen" gate
# (git diff --quiet -- bindings) could never fire because there was nothing tracked to diff.

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
